# READ THE FIELD LINE WITH ITS POLICY. This capture ran the step re-seed rule (3fe2ace,
# reverted), so the field numbers above describe a policy the tree no longer has and the
# replay rightly diverges from them: the rule made all four of this session's long runs and
# without it the same timeline holds at worst 40. The divergence is the POINT of the fixture,
# not a fidelity failure, and the same note applies to kcd_60x2_mapcycles for the same reason.
# Fidelity for the rule's own policy was checked before it was dropped: replaying this log
# with the rule armed reproduced the field's six fires at their own times and its four long
# runs (42/112/60/47 against 42/100/62/44). Record: docs/step-reseed-field-validation.md.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE GATES, and why it is worth its 4 MB: the source presents ONE frame 6 to
# 7 ms early, holds that phase about 0.65 s (40 presents), then puts it back. All four of the
# session's transients are inside this window (241, 298, 1351 and 1911 s; the only event the
# trim drops is a clean one at 1931 s). No other fixture has one, which is why a rule that
# measured clean on 43 fixtures shipped a 100-present blend run to hardware. Any future phase
# rule has to come back through this file: a rule that commits to a step faster than the
# transient reverts will blow max_worst_run, which is pinned at the transient's own length.
#
# WINDOW. The game runs from 10 s but the lock is still acquiring until 80 s, and the game
# EXITS at 1931.9 s, after which the source runs the desktop at 240 arrivals/s. On a 60 Hz
# sink the relay keeps presenting at 60/s through that, so the desktop tail is invisible in a
# present count and has to be found in the ARRIVAL rate. Cut at 120 s (40 s past the last
# acquisition disturbance) and 1925 s (6.9 s before the exit, inside 17 s of pure passthrough).
# Trimming the last 5 s moved no bound, which is the evidence those seconds were inert.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the reverted policy; re-measure deliberately when behaviour
# legitimately improves.
